course: dictionary
lesson: 1781
title: One word, more than one meaning
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Many words have more than one meaning, so the context tells you which one is meant. Climber can mean a person who climbs, or a plant that grows up walls and fences. «Climbers on Everest often carry bottles of oxygen» is about people, because people carry bottles of oxygen.
explain: Look at the clues around the word. «Watch a pea plant for a day: its thin curly tendrils feel for a stick and wrap round it» is about a plant, because a plant's tendrils wrap round a stick. Here climber means a climbing plant, like ivy, beans or roses.
explain: Use the swap check. Put your meaning into the sentence and see if it still makes sense. «High on a mountain the air is thinner, so each breath holds less oxygen» is about a person, because a plant does not climb a mountain to breathe.
fact: A climber is a person who climbs mountains, rocks or climbing walls.
fact: A climber is also a plant that grows up walls, fences or other plants, like ivy.
fact: «Climbing plant» means a plant that grows upwards, such as beans or roses.
fact: «Mountain climber» and «rock climber» are people who climb.
fact: High on mountains the air is thinner, so each breath holds less oxygen.
exercise: «High on mountains each breath holds less oxygen, so climbers breathe harder.» What is a climber in this sentence? | A bottle of oxygen | *A person who climbs | A frame in the playground | A plant that grows up a fence
exercise: «Its thin curly tendrils feel for a stick and wrap round it.» What kind of climber is this? | A mountain climber | A person in a harness | A climbing wall in a gym | *A climbing plant
exercise: Which word means a plant that grows up walls or fences? Copy the word. | summit | *climber | rope | instructor
test: «A good climber can get to the top of a rock wall.» What does climber mean here? | A tree that drops its leaves | A flower in a vase | *A person who climbs well | A bottle of oxygen
test: When ivy and roses grow up a fence, what are they called? | Gardeners | Tendrils | Frames | *Climbers
exam: Which sentence uses climber to mean a plant? | *The climber's tendrils wrapped round the fence | The climber was too heavy to lift | The climber checked her harness before the climb
